Hi Romain,

1. You can see if model selection will support that.
2. Yes, and that looks very feasible for your data.
3. Yes, and for flying CPFs this can be almost necessary, because the two states are too different for the switching process to modeled with a single stationary model.
4. If behaviors are similar, it probably won't make a difference, as the variogram is only used to generate an initial guess for the model fitting. In general, I recommend using the individual variograms if they are of good quality and a pooled variogram if they are not.

Best,
Chris

